  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "sudden memory lapse; mental blank",
      "explanation": "temporarily forgetting something you normally know well, often at an inconvenient moment"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "17611_dowasure_ex1",
      "japanese": "{名前|なまえ}を{ど忘|わす}れした。",
      "english": "I had a mental blank on the name.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "17611_dowasure_ex2",
      "japanese": "パスワードを{ど忘|わす}れして{困|こま}った。",
      "english": "I completely blanked on my password and was stuck.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "17611_dowasure_ex3",
      "japanese": "{漢字|かんじ}を{ど忘|わす}れして{書|か}けなかった。",
      "english": "I had a mental block and couldn't write the kanji.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "FORMATION:\nど (intensive prefix) + {忘|わす}れ (forgetting) → complete momentary forgetting\n\nCHARACTERISTICS:\n- Temporary - the memory usually returns\n- Often happens under pressure or when trying to recall on the spot\n- Common with names, kanji, passwords, etc.\n\nVERB FORM:\n{ど忘|わす}れする (to have a mental blank)\n\nCOMPARISON:\n- {物忘|ものわす}れ - general forgetfulness (trait)\n- {ど忘|わす}れ - momentary blank (specific instance)\n- うっかり{忘|わす}れ - careless forgetting (due to inattention)",
